  "title": "SC rejects 1978 'industry' definition for new labor code",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court of India rejected the 1978 expansive definition of 'industry' in its 2020 labor code, citing that the 1978 ruling was not valid and that the definition should be interpreted in its own text and context. The 1978 decision enabled employees in diverse jobs to have legal recourse against unfair labor practices.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court dismissed the 1978 expansive definition of 'industry' for the 2020 labor code in a majority decision.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 1978 ruling was upheld in a nine-judge bench headed by Chief Justice Surya Kant.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 1978 definition expanded workers' rights in sectors like hospitals, education, and government welfare.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
